.page test 1 check file types and compare values
.alias [

# SYNOPSIS
*test* _EXPRESSION_
*[* _EXPRESSION_ *]*

# DESCRIPTION
`test` is a gapsh builtin that evaluates _EXPRESSION_ and exits with status 0 if it is true, 1 if it is false. When written as `[` the last argument must be `]`. An empty expression is false.

# FILE TESTS
@ *-e* _FILE_
    _FILE_ exists.
@ *-f* _FILE_, *-d* _FILE_
    It is a regular file / a directory.
@ *-c* _FILE_, *-p* _FILE_
    It is a character device / a named pipe.
@ *-L* _FILE_, *-h* _FILE_
    It is a symbolic link.
@ *-s* _FILE_
    It exists and is not empty.
@ *-r* _FILE_, *-w* _FILE_, *-x* _FILE_
    It can be read / written / executed by the caller.
@ *-t* _FD_
    File descriptor _FD_ is a terminal.
@ _FILE1_ *-nt* _FILE2_, _FILE1_ *-ot* _FILE2_
    _FILE1_ is newer / older than _FILE2_.

# STRING TESTS
@ *-z* _STRING_
    The string is empty.
@ *-n* _STRING_, _STRING_
    The string is not empty.
@ _A_ = _B_, _A_ == _B_, _A_ != _B_
    The strings are equal / equal / different.
@ _A_ < _B_, _A_ > _B_
    _A_ sorts before / after _B_.

# NUMBER TESTS
@ _N_ *-eq* _M_, *-ne*, *-lt*, *-le*, *-gt*, *-ge*
    Integer comparison: equal, not equal, less, less or equal, greater, greater or equal.

# COMBINING
@ ! _EXPR_
    Not.
@ _EXPR_ *-a* _EXPR_
    And.
@ _EXPR_ *-o* _EXPR_
    Or.
@ ( _EXPR_ )
    Grouping.

Quote parentheses, `<` and `>` from the shell.

# EXIT STATUS
0 true, 1 false, 2 for a `[` without its closing `]`.

# EXAMPLES
    [ -f /Hakurei/etc/passwd ] && echo yes
    [ "$USER" = reimu ] || echo "not Reimu"
    [ $n -gt 10 -a $n -lt 20 ]

# SEE ALSO
expr(1), gapsh-language(7)
